{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for Web Awesome 3 (the open-source successor to Shoelace), default theme with the default palette. Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Named DDD colors point at fixed palette steps by role and keep the palettes distinct; the theme chrome uses Web Awesome's light (:root) and dark (.wa-dark) surface, text and brand fill tokens. Web Awesome Pro themes and palettes are commercial and excluded: only the MIT package is read. The default theme uses system font stacks, so no web font loads. Kept as DDD on purpose: font weight black (Web Awesome stops at 600), emphasized/enter/exit easing (one easing), state opacities (Web Awesome mixes colors instead), control heights (em-based, computed from padding), border size lg, and heading/body sizes.",
